{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sh6iycnjnjuek53jof432aoblecr4av76ykdw53wn4hnqnksmlaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Clean warning-free release build, and verified.\n\n## What the C library is\n\n`c_src/` is small (one TU: `src/lib.c` + `include/lib.h`), globbed by CMake into one shared object. Full exported surface from `nm -D` on the C `.so`:\n\n| Symbol | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `stbds_hash_bytes` | `size_t stbds_hash_bytes(void *p, size_t len, size_t seed)` |\n| `siphash` | `void siphash(int init)` |\n\n(`stbds_siphash_bytes` is `static` → not exported; no namespace-renaming macros in the header.)\n\n## Translation (`translation/src/lib.rs`)\n\nLiteral translation, preserving the C's quirky integer semantics rather than \"fixing\" them:\n\n- **Sign-extension bug reproduced**: `data = d[0] | (d[1]<<8) | (d[2]<<16) | (d[3]<<24)` is `int` arithmetic in C — when `d[3] >= 0x80` the shift wraps negative and the conversion to `size_t` sign-extends, clobbering the whole upper 32 bits. Same for the `case 4:` tail byte. Modeled with `i32` shifts then `as usize`.\n- **`switch` fall-through** in the 0–7 byte tail is reproduced exactly (`case k` runs when `rem >= k`).\n- `stbds_sipround` expanded verbatim (2/2/4 round schedule, rotates 13/16/17/21/32), all adds `wrapping_add`.\n- `siphash` prints through **libc `printf`** with the identical format strings (`\"  { \"`, `\"0x%02x, \"`, `\" },\\n\"`), so byte output *and* stdout buffering/flush semantics match; `mem[i] = z` truncation and the `len = 0..63` loop bound (never 64) are preserved.\n- `Cargo.toml`: `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`; exports use `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`.\n\n## Verification (independently run, not self-reported)\n\n1. **Symbol diff empty** — `nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so`s, sorted, `diff` → identical (`T siphash`, `T stbds_hash_bytes`).\n2. **Byte-identical output** — one C driver compiled twice, linked against the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`: `siphash()` for 16 `init` values (incl. negatives, `-2147483647`, `255`, `256`) plus `stbds_hash_bytes` over lengths 0–300 × 6 seeds (incl. `(size_t)-1`, `0x8000…`), all-`0xFF` / all-`0x00` / alternating-high-bit buffers, and `NULL`/len 0. **3042 lines, `cmp` clean.**\n3. **Compiler-independence** — the Rust output also matches C built at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os` **and clang -O2** (confirming the UB-dependent sign-extension path is stable, not an artifact of one build).\n\nScratch build dirs were removed; `c_src/` untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":33782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":374,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a13ecdc-c6e9-4dde-aabd-b7794063e0ee","uuid":"a28280d9-8fd4-49f5-afc4-9b21b25af82a","timestamp":"2026-08-27T16:34:03.898Z"}
